Clean-room provenance
---------------------

This cartridge was re-created from a recorded final-result baseline without
access to the prior implementation or its upstream. The implementer worked from
a specification pack — a manifest contract, measured dimensions, and reference
meshes — and from published mechanical dimensions only; no prior source, no
upstream source, and no derived code was read at any point.

It implements published mechanical interfaces:

  - the 19.05 mm keyboard key pitch, with a 0.5 mm per-side inter-cap gap
    (18.05 mm across a 1u cap, 37.10 mm across a 2u cap);
  - the Cherry MX stem: a 5.5 mm outer-diameter post carrying a cross socket of
    4.1 mm nominal arm length by 1.17 mm nominal arm width, widened by half the
    printer-fit allowance;
  - the Alps stem: a 4.5 x 3.2 mm post with a 3.2 x 1.2 mm socket, narrowed by
    the full printer-fit allowance;
  - the Box Cherry stem: a 6.0 mm square post carrying the same cross socket.

A mechanical interface dimension is not code. The profile silhouettes, the dish
curvature, the shell construction, the stem-to-keytop fusion and its support
ribs, and the legend deboss are MADFAM's own authoring.

See `docs/CLEANROOM-VERIFICATION.md` for the acceptance evidence and for the one
intentional divergence from the recorded baseline (body count).

The slug `keyv2` is retained so existing catalog references and saved
configurations keep resolving; it names this cartridge, not any prior work.
